umor is not immediately next to the previous biopsy site  all raise the possibility that this tumor may represent a third primary  The invasive carcinoma is positive for e cadherin  which is consistent with an invasive ductal carcinoma  There is no evidence of residual invasive lobular carcinoma  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  There are several cellular proliferations within the ducts in this specimen   the cells of which show negative staining with an e cadherin stain  supporting that these proliferations are lobular carcinoma in situ rather than ductal carcinoma in situ  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen  Along the anterior surface is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm flattened and slightly indurated nipple  Located 2 5cm superior to the nipple is a well healed linear scar measuring 6 5cm in length  The remaining skin surface is pink white and unremarkable  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm attached axillary tail  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm previous biopsy cavity within the mid portion of the specimen coming to 2 9cm from the overlying unremarkable free moving posterior aspect  4 5cm from the blue inked anterior soft tissue margin and 4 2cm from the scar bearing overlying skin  The cavity is empty and has a dark red to pink  smooth glistening cavity lining  The cavity borders are rubbery with focal areas of fat necrosis  No masses are grossly appreciated  Surrounding the cavity is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm area of dense lobulated pink white fibrous tissue  The remaining parenchyma is tan yellow to pink lobulated and unremarkable with no additional masses or lesions identified  Adjacent to the nipple is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm smooth walled unilocular cystic structure surrounded by slightly indurated fibrous tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm    Within the attached axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of posterior margin closest to cavity taken en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity wall   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved surrounding dense fibrous tissue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of nipple with cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Four whole lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One whole lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional axillary fat  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections of nipple and surrounding fibrous tissue  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of gray to tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the anterior  a long black stitch the lateral  and a bow tie stitch the cephalad margins  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior is blue  the superior is green and the inferior is yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm gray pink fibrous  hemorrhagic cavity which communicates with the posterior margin  The cavity is surrounded by abundant chalky tan yellow areas consistent with fat necrosis  Within the cavity wall alo