Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 13 18 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 11 53                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast cancer  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm right breast reexcision specimen with a long stitch designating new medial margin  and a short stitch designating anterior margin  The specimen is inked entirely black with the anterior half overinked with blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm previous biopsy cavity with an approximately REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm opening at the posterior aspect of the specimen  The cavity is 0 3cm from the closest anterior margin  0 5cm from the lateral margin  1 4cm from superior and inferior margin  and is at least 1 5cm from the new medial margin  The parenchyma surrounding the cavity is fibrotic with focal fat necrosis  There is no discrete  firm mass identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A C  The entire cavity from superior to inferior D F  fibrotic  hemorrhaghic area to medial margin  from superior to inferior  G  fibrotic area to superior margin  H I  fibrotic area to inferior margin  Resident  LAN WANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 57 CLINICAL DATA  45 year old female with extensive ductal carcinoma in situ and positive margins in previous biopsy  Now presents for a mastectomy  TRAM reconstruction and left breast reduction                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREASTS and AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  FOCAL RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  WITH PAGETOID SPREAD  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  BREAST  LEFT  1   PARTIAL EXCISIONS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE WITH PAGETOID SPREAD  BREAST  LEFT  2   PARTIAL EXCISIONS  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE  NOTE  14  right axillary  lymph nodes are negative for tumor  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not identified  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled  Right breast and axillary contents   is a 750 gram  modified radical mastectomy with axillary tail  The breast measures 15 x 15 x 4cm with an axillary tail of 8 x 5 x 1cm  The irregularly shaped skin surface is 14 x 8cm and is grossly unremarkable  The nipple is likewise grossly unremarkable  14 lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  ranging in size from 2 to 5mm  A 3cm well healed linear scar is present lateral and inferiorly from the nipple  2cm from the medial resection margin  1cm posterior from the skin and 1cm anterior from the deep resection margin is white  firm  fibrous nodular tissue  approximately  3 x 2 x 2cm  In the center of the specimen posterior and slightly superior to the scar is firm  microcystic breast parenchyma  Multiple cysts are present  ranging in size up to 1cm in average dimension  The smaller cysts are 2 to 4mm in diameter  Posterior and lateral to the scar is a large cystic cavity  3 x 3 x 3cm and is lined by smooth  shiny tissue  Surrounding the cavity is dense  firm  white tissue with multiple microcysts  ranging in size from 5 to 10mm in average diameter  SECTION CODE  A  lateral resection margin  B  inferior resection margin  C  posterior medial resection margin  D  posterior resection margin  middle of specimen  E  posterior lateral resection margin  F  lateral resection margin  G I  breast parenchyma  posterior medially  J R  sections near or around biopsy cavity  S  1 5cm posterior to scar  T  scar  U  nipple  V X  lymph nodes  6 3 5 respectively   Received fresh  labeled  Left breast tissue  left breast reduction  redesignated  Breast  Left  1  are four unoriented fragments of tissue weighing 230 grams  individually measuring approximately 5 x 3 x 3cm  Two pieces of tissue have triangular shaped skin ellipses focally covering part of the tissue  These skin ellipses measure 5 x 2cm and 5 x 3cm  The tissue of the four fragments is mostly adipose tissue associated with a stellate mass of white  firm  gritty  fibrous tissue with microcysts   At least 1cm in greatest dimension   Present in one fragment is a 2cm cyst in average dimension  lined by smooth  shiny tissue and containing pink fluid  Present in a second fragment is a cyst 5mm in average diameter  lined by smooth  shiny tissue and containing viscous  green yellow tissue  Present in the third fragment is a cyst 1cm in diameter  which contains clear fluid  Present in the fourth fragment is a cyst 1cm in average dimension  lined by smooth  shiny tissue and containing viscous  white tissue  A representative specimen from each piece of left breast tissue is submtted in Y Z AA and BB  Labeled  Left breast   cysts  left breast reduction     and redesignated  breast  left  2  are two fragments of breast parenchyma  measuring 3 x 2 x 1cm  Each fragment contains a mass  1cm   of firm  white  gritty focally yellow tissue admixed with adipose tissue  The parenchyma contains numerous small cysts  ranging in size up to 1 to 2mm  Representative sections of each submitted fragment are submitted in CC and DD  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Thomas Macgillivray  M D  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST and AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT  PART B  BREAST TISSUE  LEFT  PART C  BREAST   CYSTS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
