t stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm simple mastectomy specimen overlaid by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola entered by a 0 8cm in maximal diameter nipple  The nipple surface is slightly irregular and the nipple appears slightly retracted  The specimen superior half  designated by the surgeon with a short stitch  is inked black  the inferior half is inked blue and the deep resection margin is inked green  The lateral resection margin  designated by the surgeon with a long stitch  is inked yellow  Along the inferior border of the mastectomy is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse  centered by a 2 8cm long  well healed linear scar  Sectioning deeper in this area reveals a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm biopsy cavity  that extends for an approximate length of 3 5cm  along the inferior resection margin of the specimen  From this area radiate numerous white fibrous bands that reach the resection margin in multiple points  Superior to the biopsy site is an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of white  slightly firm breast parenchyma  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm white  firm area is located in the superolateral portion of the breast  scattered with yellow granules  measuring 0 2cm in maximal diameter  No lymph nodes can be dissected from the superolateral portion of the specimen  Section Code  A D  Biopsy cavity  E  Central area of firmness  F G  Superolateral area area of slight nodularity H  Nipple  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  Michael L Grossba