terone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm segment of fibrofatty breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular 2 5cm firm tan white mass  which is 0 1cm from the closest inked margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1 and frozen section  2  The remainder is submitted entirely in cassettes A through G  Frozen section  1 submitted as H  and frozen section  2 is submitted in cassette I  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
