Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 12 13 CLINICAL DATA  Known invasive carcinoma of the right breast  now right lumpectomy with sentinel node mapping                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY BASED ON EXAMINATION OF ROUTINE SECTIONS  IMMUNOCYTOCHEMICAL STAINS FOR CYTOKERATIN   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CAM REMOVED_DATE ARE NEGATIVE  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17 31 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right Sentinel Node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm lymph node with a small amount of attached soft tissue  bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  The lymph node was then thawed and resubmitted in toto into Cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right Breast Lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibroadipose tissue  needle guidewire in place  According to the information provided by the surgeon  the short stitch is orienting the superior margin  the long stitch orienting the lateral margin  The specimen has an anterior skin ellipse of REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  which contains a well healed scar of 4 5cm  The superior surface of the specimen is inked black  The inferior surface is inked blue  The specimen is sliced from lateral to medial  The slices reveal a fibrous  white  rather soft area  focally patchy  which abuts the inferior posterior margin in approximately