noting the medial anterior aspect which is inked green  two stitches denoting the superior anterior aspect which is inked blue  three stitches denoting the lateral anterior aspect which is inked black and four stitches which are not grossly identified on the specimen which is inked orange and denotes the inferior anterior aspect  The deep margin is inked red  The specimen is sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a biopsy cavity which is open to the superior and medial aspects adjacent to the skin ellipse  The REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm biopsy cavity contains an indurated nodular lining which is within 0 4cm of the deep margin and directly opens to the superior and medial anterior margin  The remaining parenchyma has a moderate amount of dense tan white fibrous tissue admixed with a small amount of tan yellow adipose tissue  Multiple small cysts ranging up to 0 4cm in greatest dimension are identified within the firm focally nodular dense fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  G  Biopsy cavity to posterior lateral margin H  Cavity to medial margin I  Cavity to superior margin J  Biopsy cavity to lateral anterior and skin margin K  Representative section away from biopsy cavity  Gross Description by  KRISTEN SMITH Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE RIGHT AXILLA   HIGHEST    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT AXILLA    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 MAY 98 at 09 50 CLINICAL DATA  Pregnant female  8cm mass of breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  WITH MULTIFOCAL MICROINVASION  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE RESECTION MARGINS  Note  All blocks contain ductal carcinoma in situ  Occasional foci of stromal invasion are seen  the largest of which spans 1mm  While this particular focus is distant from resection margins  other areas suspicious for stromal invasion are close  1mm   to margins  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  15 MAY 98 at 18 03 Consulting Pathologist s   Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lump   are two portions of firm breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimens are inked and sectioned to reveal focally firm fibrofatty tissue with multifocal white calcification with no discrete lesion  Representative sections of the smaller portion with calcifications are frozen as FX  1 and are saved for Cox 5  The remainder of the small case is entirely submitted in cassettes A B  The larger portion is entirely submitted in cassettes C H  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE WITH CALCIFICATIONS  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
