 protein with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass   is a 6 x 3 x 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  Sectioning reveals an ill defined  firm  white  focally gritty area  2 5cm in diameter  extending to the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue for estrogen receptor studies is taken  Representative sections submitted in A through J  Resident  Jane M  Yang  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  Edwin Post Maynard  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
