 Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 30     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Invasive carcinoma is not recognized in the sections stained for hormone receptor proteins  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a localizing wire in place  Sectioning reveals many small areas of yellow calcification and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  tan gray  poorly defined area  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1  The suspicious area is submitted in A through D  the remainder entirely in E through K  Resident  George O  Kucyj  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  AWAIT PERMANENTS TO RULE OUT INVASION  O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
