Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 41 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  45    WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   55    CRIBRIFORM TYPE  3  RADIAL SCAR  SLIDE G   4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The infiltrating ductal carcinoma  slide B  maximum diameter 0 6cm   as well as the DCIS are present at inked surgical resection margins and are associated with microcalcifications  No definite vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 17 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 36 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy with needle localization wire   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a needle localizing wire in place  and an accompanying specimen X ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal adipose tissue interspersed with white  rubbery  fibrous tissue  There is no grossly suspicious lesion for infiltrating carcinoma identified  No frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted with possible microcalcifications in A through F and the remaining tissue entirely in G through Q  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  GROSS TUMOR MASS NOT IDENTIFIED  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY WITH NEEDLE LOCALIZATION   report_end  , Unchecked.
